{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block body %}
<section>
  <h1>A security engineer for your Supabase app.</h1>
  <p class="sub">Checks every push. Opens small fixes with a test. Opt-in.</p>
</section>

<section class="cols">
  <div>
    <h2>What it checks</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>tables without RLS</li>
      <li>secret keys in client code</li>
      <li>write-anything policies</li>
      <li>public storage buckets</li>
      <li>unsafe security-definer functions</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h2>What it never does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>read your data</li>
      <li>write to your database</li>
      <li>touch repos you didn't pick</li>
      <li>use a leaked key it finds</li>
      <li>open guessed fixes</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Example fix PR</h2>
  <p class="small">A real rendered PR body — every fix ships with the same shape: what an attacker can do, a proof you can run, the change, a test, and a way to undo.</p>
  <pre>Anyone on the internet can read and write every row in
`posts` right now.

## Prove it yourself (30 seconds)

curl -sI "https://yourapp.supabase.co/rest/v1/posts?select=*" \
  -H "apikey: <your anon key>" \
  -H "Prefer: count=exact" -H "Range: 0-0" | grep -i content-range

## What this PR changes
- supabase/migrations/…_vibeguard_rls_posts.sql
- supabase/tests/vibeguard_posts.test.sql

## How to test
supabase start && supabase test db</pre>
</section>

<section>
  <a class="btn" href="{{ install_url }}">Install</a>
  <p class="small" style="margin-top:12px">Installs on the repos you choose. A config PR arrives within 15 minutes. Uninstall any time — your findings are deleted after 30 days.</p>
  <p class="small"><a href="{{ root }}scoreboard/">Scoreboard</a></p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
